{"id":"mahabharata-11-020","work":"mahabharata","part":11,"partName":"स्त्रीपर्व","partNameEn":"Stri Parva","unit":20,"title":"विंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 20 · Abhimanyu and Uttara","summary":{"en":"Gandhari turns to Abhimanyu, whose body lies with the young bride Uttara weeping by it, and describes the boy's youth and his death. She mourns Lakshmana, Duryodhana's son, and Kamboja's king, and many others.","kn":"ಗಾಂಧಾರಿ ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯುವಿನ ಬಳಿ ತಿರುಗಿ ಯುವ ವಧು ಉತ್ತರೆ ಅಳುತ್ತಿರುವುದನ್ನು ತೋರಿಸಿ ಬಾಲಕನ ಯೌವನ ಮತ್ತು ಸಾವನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಮಗ ಲಕ್ಷ್ಮಣ, ಕಾಂಬೋಜ ರಾಜ ಮತ್ತು ಅನೇಕರಿಗಾಗಿ ದುಃಖಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"गान्धारी अभिमन्यु की ओर मुड़ती हैं, जिसके शव के पास नवविवाहिता उत्तरा रो रही है, और उस बालक के यौवन तथा मृत्यु का वर्णन करती हैं। वे दुर्योधन के पुत्र लक्ष्मण, काम्बोज राजा और अनेक अन्य के लिए शोक करती हैं।","te":"గాంధారి అభిమన్యుని వద్దకు తిరిగి అతని శవం వద్ద యువ వధువు ఉత్తర ఏడుస్తున్నదని చూపి బాలుని యౌవనాన్ని, మరణాన్ని వర్ణిస్తుంది. దుర్యోధనుని కొడుకు లక్ష్మణుని, కాంభోజ రాజును, అనేకులను తలచి దుఃఖిస్తుంది.","ta":"காந்தாரி அபிமன்யுவிடம் திரும்பி, அவன் உடலருகே இளம் மணப்பெண் உத்தரை அழுவதைக் காட்டி அச்சிறுவனின் இளமையையும் மரணத்தையும் விவரிக்கிறாள். துரியோதனனின் மகன் லட்சுமணன், காம்போஜ மன்னன் மற்றும் பலருக்காகத் துயருறுகிறாள்.","ml":"അഭിമന്യുവിന്റെ ശരീരത്തിനരികിൽ, യുവവധു ഉത്തര കരഞ്ഞിരിക്കുന്നത് കണ്ട് ഗാന്ധാരി അദ്ദേഹത്തിലേക്ക് തിരിയുന്നു; ആ ബാലന്റെ യൗവനവും മരണവും അവൾ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ദുര്യോധനന്റെ പുത്രൻ ലക്ഷ്മണൻ, കംബോജരാജാവ് എന്നിവരെയും മറ്റു പലരെയും അവൾ ഓർത്ത് വിലപിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 11.20; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 17 2017","sections":[{"title":"स्त्रीविलापपर्व","titleEn":"Strivilapa Parva (Lament of the women)","verses":[{"text":"गान्धार्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Gandhari said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अध्यर्धगुणमाहुर्यं बले शौर्ये च माधव ।\nपित्रा त्वया च दाशार्ह दृप्तं सिंहमिवोत्कटम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhava, descendant of Dasharha, they called him one and a half times as great in strength and valor as you and his father, proud and fierce like a lion."}},{"n":2,"text":"यो बिभेद चमूमेको मम पुत्रस्य दुर्भिदाम् ।\nस भूत्वा मृत्युरन्येषां स्वयं मृत्युवशं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who alone broke through the hard-to-break army of my son became Death for others and has himself gone under the power of Death."}},{"n":3,"text":"तस्योपलक्षये कृष्ण कार्ष्णेरमिततेजसः ।\nअभिमन्योर्हतस्यापि प्रभा नैवोपशाम्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, I see that the radiance of Abhimanyu, the immeasurably splendid son of Arjuna, does not fade even though he is slain."}},{"n":4,"text":"एषा विराटदुहिता स्नुषा गाण्डीवधन्वनः ।\nआर्ता बाला पतिं वीरं शोच्या शोचत्यनिन्दिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here is Virata's daughter, the daughter-in-law of the wielder of Gandiva, a pitiable girl in distress, blameless, mourning her hero husband."}},{"n":5,"text":"तमेषा हि समासाद्य भार्या भर्तारमन्तिके ।\nविराटदुहिता कृष्ण पाणिना परिमार्जति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, this wife, Virata's daughter, has come near her husband and wipes him with her hand."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्य वक्त्रमुपाघ्राय सौभद्रस्य यशस्विनी ।\nविबुद्धकमलाकारं कम्बुवृत्तशिरोधरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Smelling the face of the glorious son of Subhadra, which was like an opened lotus, his neck round like a conch,"}},{"n":7,"text":"काम्यरूपवती चैषा परिष्वजति भामिनी ।\nलज्जमाना पुरेवैनं माध्वीकमदमूर्छिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"this lovely, beautiful woman embraces him, shy as before, dazed as if by honey wine."}},{"n":8,"text":"तस्य क्षतजसंदिग्धं जातरूपपरिष्कृतम् ।\nविमुच्य कवचं कृष्ण शरीरमभिवीक्षते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Removing the armor from his gold-decked body smeared with blood, Krishna, she gazes at it."}},{"n":9,"text":"अवेक्षमाणा तं बाला कृष्ण त्वामभिभाषते ।\nअयं ते पुण्डरीकाक्ष सदृशाक्षो निपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The girl, looking at him, says to you: \"Lotus-eyed one, this one, with eyes like yours, is struck down."}},{"n":10,"text":"बले वीर्ये च सदृशस्तेजसा चैव तेऽनघ ।\nरूपेण च तवात्यर्थं शेते भुवि निपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Faultless one, he was like you in strength, valor and splendor, and exceedingly like you in beauty; he lies fallen on the ground."}},{"n":11,"text":"अत्यन्तसुकुमारस्य राङ्कवाजिनशायिनः ।\nकच्चिदद्य शरीरं ते भूमौ न परितप्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You who were so very tender and slept on deerskin, does your body not suffer now on the ground?"}},{"n":12,"text":"मातङ्गभुजवर्ष्माणौ ज्याक्षेपकठिनत्वचौ ।\nकाञ्चनाङ्गदिनौ शेषे निक्षिप्य विपुलौ भुजौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Your two broad arms, like elephant trunks, hard with the pull of the bowstring, wearing golden armlets, you have laid down and sleep."}},{"n":13,"text":"व्यायम्य बहुधा नूनं सुखसुप्तः श्रमादिव ।\nएवं विलपतीमार्तां न हि मामभिभाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely you have exercised in many ways and sleep happily, as if from weariness. Though I lament in distress, you do not speak to me."}},{"n":14,"text":"आर्यामार्य सुभद्रां त्वमिमांश्च त्रिदशोपमान् ।\nपितॄन्मां चैव दुःखार्तां विहाय क्व गमिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Noble one, leaving the noble Subhadra, these fathers like gods, and me, afflicted with grief, where will you go?\""}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्य शोणितसंदिग्धान्केशानुन्नाम्य पाणिना ।\nउत्सङ्गे वक्त्रमाधाय जीवन्तमिव पृच्छति ।\nस्वस्रीयं वासुदेवस्य पुत्रं गाण्डीवधन्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She lifts his hair, smeared with blood, with her hand, puts his face in her lap, and asks as if he were alive Vasudeva's nephew, the son of the wielder of Gandiva:"}},{"n":16,"text":"कथं त्वां रणमध्यस्थं जघ्नुरेते महारथाः ।\nधिगस्तु क्रूरकर्तॄंस्तान्कृपकर्णजयद्रथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How did those great charioteers strike you down in the midst of battle? Shame on those cruel doers, Kripa, Karna and Jayadratha,"}},{"n":17,"text":"द्रोणद्रौणायनी चोभौ यैरसि व्यसनीकृतः ।\nरथर्षभाणां सर्वेषां कथमासीत्तदा मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"and both Drona and Drona's son, by whom you were brought to this misfortune. What was in the minds of all those chariot-bulls then?"}},{"n":18,"text":"बालं त्वां परिवार्यैकं मम दुःखाय जघ्नुषाम् ।\nकथं नु पाण्डवानां च पाञ्चालानां च पश्यताम् ।\nत्वं वीर निधनं प्राप्तो नाथवान्सन्ननाथवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surrounding you, a boy, alone, they killed you, to my grief. How, hero, did you meet death like one without protector, though you had protectors, while the Pandavas and Panchalas looked on?"}},{"n":19,"text":"दृष्ट्वा बहुभिराक्रन्दे निहतं त्वामनाथवत् ।\nवीरः पुरुषशार्दूलः कथं जीवति पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing you killed like one without protector amid many in the clamor, how does the hero Pandava, tiger among men, stay alive?"}},{"n":20,"text":"न राज्यलाभो विपुलः शत्रूणां वा पराभवः ।\nप्रीतिं दास्यति पार्थानां त्वामृते पुष्करेक्षण ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Neither a great gain of kingdom nor the defeat of enemies will bring joy to the sons of Pritha without you, lotus-eyed one."}},{"n":21,"text":"तव शस्त्रजिताँल्लोकान्धर्मेण च दमेन च ।\nक्षिप्रमन्वागमिष्यामि तत्र मां प्रतिपालय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By dharma and self-control I will soon follow you to the worlds you have won by weapons; wait for me there."}},{"n":22,"text":"दुर्मरं पुनरप्राप्ते काले भवति केनचित् ।\nयदहं त्वां रणे दृष्ट्वा हतं जीवामि दुर्भगा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It is hard for anyone to die before the time has come, since I, unfortunate, live on after seeing you slain in battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"कामिदानीं नरव्याघ्र श्लक्ष्णया स्मितया गिरा ।\nपितृलोके समेत्यान्यां मामिवामन्त्रयिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Now, tiger among men, whom will you call to you with soft smiling words when you meet me in the world of the fathers, as you did me?"}},{"n":24,"text":"नूनमप्सरसां स्वर्गे मनांसि प्रमथिष्यसि ।\nपरमेण च रूपेण गिरा च स्मितपूर्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely you will captivate the minds of the apsarases in heaven with your supreme beauty and your smiling speech."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्राप्य पुण्यकृताँल्लोकानप्सरोभिः समेयिवान् ।\nसौभद्र विहरन्काले स्मरेथाः सुकृतानि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having reached the worlds of the righteous and met the apsarases, son of Subhadra, when you are at play, remember my good deeds."}},{"n":26,"text":"एतावानिह संवासो विहितस्ते मया सह ।\nषण्मासान्सप्तमे मासि त्वं वीर निधनं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This much time together was given to you with me: six months, and in the seventh month, hero, you met your end.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"इत्युक्तवचनामेतामपकर्षन्ति दुःखिताम् ।\nउत्तरां मोघसंकल्पां मत्स्यराजकुलस्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The women of the Matsya king's family draw away the grieving Uttara, whose hopes were in vain, as she said this."}},{"n":28,"text":"उत्तरामपकृष्यैनामार्तामार्ततराः स्वयम् ।\nविराटं निहतं दृष्ट्वा क्रोशन्ति विलपन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having drawn Uttara away, those women, themselves in greater distress, seeing Virata slain, cry out and lament."}},{"n":29,"text":"द्रोणास्त्रशरसंकृत्तं शयानं रुधिरोक्षितम् ।\nविराटं वितुदन्त्येते गृध्रगोमायुवायसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vultures, jackals and crows tear at Virata as he lies cut by Drona's weapon arrows and drenched in blood."}},{"n":30,"text":"वितुद्यमानं विहगैर्विराटमसितेक्षणाः ।\nन शक्नुवन्ति विवशा निवर्तयितुमातुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dark-eyed women, helpless and distressed, cannot drive away the birds that are tearing at Virata."}},{"n":31,"text":"आसामातपतप्तानामायासेन च योषिताम् ।\nश्रमेण च विवर्णानां रूपाणां विगतं वपुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bodies of these women, scorched by the sun and wearied by exertion, have lost their bright color."}},{"n":32,"text":"उत्तरं चाभिमन्युं च काम्बोजं च सुदक्षिणम् ।\nशिशूनेतान्हतान्पश्य लक्ष्मणं च सुदर्शनम् ।\nआयोधनशिरोमध्ये शयानं पश्य माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at Uttara, Abhimanyu and Sudakshina the Kamboja, these young ones slain, and look at Lakshmana and Sudarshana. Madhava, look at them lying in the front of the battlefield."}}]}]}